cff-version: 1.2.0
title: CelFDrive
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the versioned Zenodo release. The
  associated journal article will be added when it is published.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-25'
abstract: >-
  CelFDrive is software for automated detection of rare cellular events that
  drives high-resolution 3D microscopy acquisition. It integrates deep-learning
  cell classification from auxiliary low-magnification fluorescence images,
  detecting cells of interest with a fine-tuned YOLO11x object-detection model
  and automatically steering the microscope to image them at high resolution.
  It has been deployed on lattice light-sheet and spinning-disk confocal
  systems. Adapting CelFDrive to another microscope-control system requires
  microscope-specific coordinate, capture-command, and hardware-safety
  validation.

